Connector plugin jars distributed as release assets

Tapstate loads connector plugins as separate, independently licensed artifacts;
none of them are part of this source tree or of any Tapstate binary. For
convenience, prebuilt connector jars are published as assets on the
"connectors-preview" release so the online-runtime quickstart can be run without
building the connector repositories first. Those jars are shaded and carry their
own drivers on an isolated class loader:

  * mysql-connector.jar bundles Oracle MySQL Connector/J 8.0, licensed under
    GPL-2.0 with the Universal FOSS Exception. That exception is what permits its
    distribution alongside Apache-2.0 licensed software.

  * mongodb-connector.jar bundles the MongoDB Java driver (Apache-2.0) and other
    Apache-2.0 and BSD licensed components.

Each jar carries the full license text of its bundled dependencies under
META-INF/. Their licenses govern those jars; they do not alter the Apache-2.0
license of Tapstate itself.

